    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99-a1-a9">

                <pb facs="0293" n="235" xml:id="pg235"/>


                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexican Legation in the United States
                                of America</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 6, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>In my letter to you on the 25th of May last, in reply to yours of the 21st of the
                    same month, I informed you I had sent your note of that date to the government
                    of the republic, in accordance with your wishes. This day I received a note from
                    Mr. Lerdo de Tejada, minister of foreign relations and government of the
                    republic, dated in Chihuahua, the 6th of July last, and numbered 289, containing
                    the answer of our government to your offer of services.</p>
                <p>In accordance with instructions to me in that note, I send you a copy of it.</p>
                <p>I embrace the occasion to renew the assurances of my most attentive
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. ROMERO</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Señor Don <hi rendition="#small-caps">Antonio Lopez de Santa Anna</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">New York</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
